# #262 (b11, owner's log 2026-11-10): Hold switched on and off while a video
# plays with Repeat All gave about 3 s with no new picture ("audio stands
# still", "thread late 2078 ms", "audio jumped", "seek's first picture
# 973 ms"). Cause: the Hold change flushed playback's queue ahead
# (audio_flush_and_reload_tracks()), and the reload of the wrap (the same
# file again) read its metadata on the audio thread while holding the id3
# lock (playback.c audio_load_track(), the buffer-full branch: a long
# video never fits, so it always takes that branch), through a storage
# power-up. The video thread reads the playing track through that lock
# every turn (vplayer.c audio_us()/audio_handle()), so it stood still for
# the whole wake and the parse.
#
# Here: a 12 min episode (the soak fixture) with Repeat All and an audio
# buffer smaller than the file (stor_buffer: as on the device, where a
# long video never fits), storage that powers off after a short hold and
# wakes in 2 s (a disk's typical wake). Hold goes on and off three times,
# each time after the storage powered off.
#  h0-h1  each Hold change is logged with its time and its flush; the
#         wrap's tags are never read from the file again (no "Read
#         metadata" for it: the refetch copies them from the buffered
#         file, so nothing slow runs under the lock); the video thread is
#         never late by a wake (1500 ms or more) and the audio clock never
#         stands still.
# What the simulator can't show: the 2 s itself. Its open() powers the
# storage up before the lock is taken and host reads are instant, so the
# old code was not late here either; the "Read metadata" lines are the
# old code's read under the lock (seen with a temporary trace in the
# buffer-full branch, 2026-11-10). The device row holdv measures the time.
# Repeat semantics (Hold on: the end is the end; off: the wrap) stay with
# ipodui-p19-video-hold.script.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui-video scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-b12-holdv.script
# needs: video
# needs: soak
# golden: skip
# timeout: 240
# fulls-extra: 3   (the menu under the video at play_files, video_screen and the stop)
# logbetween: h0 h1 video hold on t=\d+ ms flush=1
# logbetween: h0 h1 video hold off t=\d+ ms flush=1
# logbetween: h0 h1 no Read metadata for /.rockbox/soak/holdv.m4v
# logbetween: h0 h1 no video: thread late \(ms past its wait, audio ms\) \((1[5-9]\d\d|[2-9]\d{3}|\d{5,}),
# logbetween: h0 h1 no video: audio stands still
# nolog: video error page
# nolog: video: stopped, BCM given back
# nolog: CPU FALLBACK
wait 4000
mkdir /.rockbox/soak    # hidden: never in the library
copy ../../build/soak-fixtures/soak.m4v /.rockbox/soak/holdv.m4v
play_files /.rockbox/soak/holdv.m4v   # playback's buffer exists only after a first play
wait 1500
audio_stop
wait 500
stor_buffer 3000000     # smaller than the file, as any long video on the unit
stor_tune 1500 500      # off 1.5 s after the last access
stor_pwrup 2000         # a disk's wake
repeat all
video_screen /.rockbox/soak/holdv.m4v
wait 6000
expect_video 20 playing
ab_mark h0
stor_expect off 15000
hold_switch on
wait 3000
stor_expect off 15000
hold_switch off
wait 4000
stor_expect off 15000
hold_switch on
wait 3000
stor_expect off 15000
hold_switch off
wait 4000
stor_expect off 15000
hold_switch on
wait 3000
stor_expect off 15000
hold_switch off
wait 5000
expect_video 200 playing
ab_mark h1
key MENU
wait 2000
repeat off
stor_buffer 0
stor_pwrup 300
shot after              # the list again (shots.sh wants one)
rm_file /.rockbox/soak/holdv.m4v
